    "\n",
    "### Basic Block vs Bottleneck Block\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Basic Block (ResNet18/34)\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses two 3×3 convolutions.\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "3×3 Conv\n",
    "3×3 Conv\n",
    "Skip Add\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Bottleneck Block (ResNet50+)\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "1×1 → 3×3 → 1×1\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Purpose:\n",
    "\n",
    "* reduce computation\n",
    "* increase depth efficiently\n",
    "\n",
    "| Layer    | Purpose            |\n",
    "| -------- | ------------------ |\n",
    "| 1×1 Conv | Reduce channels    |\n",
    "| 3×3 Conv | Feature extraction |\n",
    "| 1×1 Conv | Restore channels   |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Identity Mapping\n",
    "\n",
    "If input and output dimensions match:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "y = F(x) + x\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Otherwise:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "y = F(x) + W_s x\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $W_s$ is a projection matrix (usually 1×1 convolution).\n",
    "$$\n",
    "y=F(x)+W_sx\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "## Cat vs Dog Classifier\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose we classify:\n",
    "\n",
    "* cat\n",
    "* dog\n",
    "* horse\n",
    "\n",
    "Input image:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "224 × 224 × 3\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Initial Convolution\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "7×7 Conv + ReLU\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Extracts:\n",
    "\n",
    "* edges\n",
    "* textures\n",
    "* low-level features\n",
    "\n",
    "### Residual Blocks\n",
    "\n",
    "Residual blocks learn:\n",
    "\n",
    "* shapes\n",
    "* object parts\n",
    "* high-level patterns\n",
    "\n",
    "Example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "Input Feature Map\n",
    "      │\n",
    "Conv Layers learn residual F(x)\n",
    "      │\n",
    "Add original input x\n",
    "      │\n",
    "Output = F(x) + x\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "If convolutions learn nothing useful:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "F(x) \\approx 0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Then:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "H(x) \\approx x\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Meaning:\n",
    "\n",
    "> the network can simply preserve information instead of damaging it.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is one of the key reasons ResNet works.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Example Workthough\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x = 5\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Desired mapping:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "H(x)=8\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of directly learning 8, the block learns:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "F(x)=3\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Then:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "H(x)=F(x)+x=3+5=8\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Learning residuals is often easier than learning full mappings.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Charecterstics\n",
    "\n",
    "### Advantages\n",
    "\n",
    "| Advantage                  | Explanation                            |\n",
    "| -------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n",
    "| Enables very deep networks | 100+ layers possible                   |\n",
    "| Better gradient flow       | Skip connections help                  |\n",
    "| Higher accuracy            | Excellent performance                  |\n",
    "| Easier optimization        | Residual learning simplifies training  |\n",
    "| Reusable features          | Identity mapping preserves information |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Disadvantages\n",
    "\n",
    "| Limitation         | Explanation                  |\n",
    "| ------------------ | ---------------------------- |\n",
    "| Computational cost | Deep models require GPUs     |\n",
    "| Memory usage       | Large models consume RAM     |\n",
    "| Overfitting risk   | On small datasets            |\n",
    "| Slower inference   | Compared to lightweight CNNs |\n",
    "\n",
    "### ResNet vs Traditional CNN\n",
    "\n",
    "| Traditional CNN            | ResNet                  |\n",
    "| -------------------------- | ----------------------- |\n",
    "| Learns direct mapping      | Learns residual mapping |\n",
    "| Difficult at large depth   | Easier to train         |\n",
    "| Vanishing gradients common | Skip connections help   |\n",
    "| Limited depth              | Extremely deep possible |\n",
    "\n",
    "Imagine climbing stairs.\n",
    "\n",
    "Traditional CNN:\n",
    "\n",
    "* every layer must completely transform information\n",
    "\n",
    "ResNet:\n",
    "\n",
    "* layers only learn the “difference” needed\n",
    "* unchanged information can pass directly\n",
    "\n",
    "This makes learning easier.\n",
    "\n",
    "# Dense Convolutional Network\n",
    "\n",
    "**DenseNet** (Dense Convolutional Network) is a deep learning architecture introduced in the paper:\n",
    "\n",
    "> [Densely Connected Convolutional Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1608.06993)\n",
    "\n",
    "by Gao Huang and collaborators.\n",
    "\n",
    "DenseNet improves information flow between layers by connecting **every layer to every other layer** in a feed-forward manner. Instead of a layer receiving input only from the previous layer, each layer receives the outputs of **all previous layers**.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Core Idea of Dense Connectivity\n",
    "\n",
    "In a traditional CNN:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_l = H_l(x_{l-1})\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Layer (l) only uses the previous layer output.\n",
    "\n",
    "In DenseNet:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_l = H_l([x_0, x_1, x_2, ..., x_{l-1}])\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "* $x_l$ = output of layer ($l$)\n",
    "* $[]$ = concatenation operation\n",
    "* $H_l$ = operations like BatchNorm + ReLU + Conv\n",
    "\n",
    "This means:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Feature maps from earlier layers are reused\n",
    "* Gradient flows directly to earlier layers\n",
    "* Vanishing gradient problem is reduced\n",
    "* Parameters become more efficient\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Imagine students in a classroom.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Traditional CNN**\n",
    "\n",
    "Each student only talks to the next student.\n",
    "\n",
    "**DenseNet**\n",
    "\n",
    "Every student shares notes with every future student.\n",
    "\n",
    "Result:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Better information sharing\n",
    "* Less forgetting\n",
    "* Faster learning\n",
    "\n",
    "That is the intuition behind DenseNet.\n",
    "\n",
    "## DenseNet Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "Typical DenseNet pipeline:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Input\n",
    "2. Initial Convolution\n",
    "3. Dense Block 1\n",
    "4. Transition Layer\n",
    "5. Dense Block 2\n",
    "6. Transition Layer\n",
    "7. Dense Block 3\n",
    "8. Classification Layer\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dense Connectivity Visualization\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose we have 4 layers.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Traditional CNN\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "x0 → x1 → x2 → x3 → x4\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "#### DenseNet\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "x0 → x1\n",
    " │  ↘\n",
    " │    x2\n",
    " │  ↗ ↘\n",
    " │ ↗    x3\n",
    " ↓↘ ↗ ↘\n",
    "    x4\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Every layer receives inputs from all previous layers.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dense Block\n",
    "\n",
    "The main building unit in DenseNet is the **Dense Block**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Inside a dense block:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Each layer concatenates all previous outputs\n",
    "* Feature maps grow continuously\n",
    "\n",
    "Layer 3 input:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "[x_0, x_1, x_2]\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Layer 4 input:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "[x_0, x_1, x_2, x_3]\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "### Growth Rate ($k$)\n",
    "\n",
    "DenseNet introduces a parameter called **growth rate**.\n",
    "\n",
    "It controls how many new feature maps each layer contributes.\n",
    "\n",
    "If:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Growth rate (k = 12)\n",
    "* Each layer adds 12 feature maps\n",
    "\n",
    "Then feature size increases gradually.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Layer   | Feature Maps |\n",
    "| ------- | ------------ |\n",
    "| Input   | 24           |\n",
    "| Layer 1 | 24 + 12 = 36 |\n",
    "| Layer 2 | 36 + 12 = 48 |\n",
    "| Layer 3 | 48 + 12 = 60 |\n",
    "\n",
    "This controlled growth keeps the model efficient.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Transition Layers\n",
    "\n",
    "Because feature maps keep increasing, DenseNet uses **transition layers** between dense blocks.\n",
    "\n",
    "A transition layer contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Batch Normalization\n",
    "2. ($1 \\times 1$) convolution\n",
    "3. Average Pooling\n",
    "\n",
    "Purpose:\n",
    "\n",
    "* Reduce feature map size\n",
    "* Compress channels\n",
    "* Control memory usage\n",
    "\n",
    "### DenseNet Bottleneck Layer\n",
    "\n",
    "DenseNet often uses a bottleneck structure:\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "BN → ReLU → 1×1 Conv\n",
    "        ↓\n",
    "BN → ReLU → 3×3 Conv\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Why?\n",
    "\n",
    "* ($1 \\times 1$) convolution reduces channels\n",
    "* Makes computation cheaper\n",
    "\n",
    "This version is called **DenseNet-BC**:\n",
    "\n",
    "* B = Bottleneck\n",
    "* C = Compression\n"
   ]
